    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td rowspan="1" bgcolor=LightGray><b> PB3D finalize </b></td><td colspan="2"> the Richardson summary is written (see term_rich()), the variables are deallocated, MPI is stopped (see stop_mpi()) and the output files are closed (see close_output()) </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    With the command-line option <tt>--jump_to_sol</tt>, at the level \c rich_restart_lvl, the equilibrium and perturbation drivers read the grids, the flux equilibrium quantities (and, for HELENA, the metric equilibrium quantities and the vectorial perturbation quantities) and the magnetic integrals back from the HDF5 output, instead of calculating them.
    The solution driver then reads the vacuum response back as well, for a free boundary.
    The magnetic integrals of that level have to be present in the HDF5 output; otherwise PB3D stops (see open_output()).


    \section overview_POST POST Overview
    The POST program for post-processing of PB3D results consists of just one driver.
        - In the first part, everything is set up (see init_post()):
            - This includes reading the variables written to HDF5 by PB3D, among which the vacuum response for a free boundary.
            - Furthermore, the output grids are created.
            - Also, 1-D flux plots are produced, which are part of the plots that PB3D is able to produce (see \c plot_flux_q, \c plot_resonance and \c plot_magn_grid in table \ref output_plots_tab "3" in \ref page_outputs).
            - If the solution is needed, the eigenvalues and the Fourier harmonics of the eigenvectors are plotted, and, for a free boundary, the vacuum potential (see \c plot_vac_pot in table \ref output_plots_tab "3" in \ref page_outputs).
        - After that, new outputs are calculated and plotted (see run_driver_post()):
            - Quantities are calculated on the output grids.
            - Using these, plots are first produced that do not depend on the solution vector from PB3D, and are also part of the plots that PB3D is able to produce (see \c plot_B, \c plot_J, \c plot_kappa in table \ref output_plots_tab "3" in \ref page_outputs).
            - Finally, other plots are produced that do depend on these (see \c plot_sol_xi, \c plot_sol_Q, \c plot_E_rec in table \ref output_plots_tab "3" in \ref page_outputs).

    POST also knows the concept of equilibrium jobs, but not that of perturbation jobs (see \ref overview_jobs).
    This is necessary for larger outputs that quickly overflow memory.
    The HDF5 output files are updated at every equilibrium job, but, with reasonable safety, they can already be looked at in a visualizer.
*/
